{
  "source_note": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 is Amendment 2 to the Supplier Policy, issued on 2026-08-14 by L. Moreno and effective 2026-09-01. It tightens the acceptance criteria for UN 38.3 battery certificates following an incoming test failure in July 2026. The amendment is current as of today, 26 October 2026.",
  "pages": [
    {
      "slug": "amd-sup-2026-02",
      "type": "policy",
      "title": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 Amendment 2 to the Supplier Policy",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 version 1.0 was authored by L. Moreno on 2026-08-14 and became effective on 2026-09-01 under the ownership of the Northbridge Cycles Purchase department.",
          "quote": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 Version 1.0 Effective 2026-09-01 Owner Purchase department, Northbridge Cycles Status CURRENT Classification INTERNAL Version history Version Date Author Change 1.0 2026-08-14 L. Moreno Issued",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Amendment 2 to the Supplier Policy",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "With effect from 1 September 2026, POL-SUP-003 §4.4 is replaced so that a UN 38.3 certificate is accepted only if issued within the last 12 months and its valid-to date is at least 60 days after the order placement date.",
          "quote": "With effect from 1 September 2026, Supplier Policy POL-SUP-003 §4.4 is replaced by the following: \"A UN 38.3 certificate is accepted only if it was issued within the last 12 months, and its valid-to date is at least 60 days after the date the order is placed.\"",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "Certificates meeting the former rule of being issued within 24 months and unexpired count as no certificate for new orders placed from 1 September 2026, while orders released before that date remain unaffected.",
          "quote": "A certificate that meets the old rule (issued within 24 months and not expired) but not the new one counts as no certificate for new orders from 1 September 2026. Orders released before that date are not affected.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "The policy amendment was introduced because a battery pack lot from a supplier with a 22-month-old test report failed Northbridge's incoming abuse test in July 2026 after the underlying cell maker changed.",
          "quote": "In July 2026 a battery pack lot from a supplier with a 22-month-old test report failed our own incoming abuse test. The cell maker had changed in the meantime.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "2. Why",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "Purchase staff must inspect the certificate's issue date and valid-to date against the new 12-month issuance and 60-day expiry buffer rule before raising an order for a lithium-cell part.",
          "quote": "Before raising an order for a lithium-cell part, check the certificate's issue date and its valid-to date against the new rule.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "The senior buyer must run the certificate-expiry report (MAN-PUR-72 §22.6) on the first working day of each month with a 90-day window and contact every supplier whose UN 38.3 certificate expires within that window.",
          "quote": "The senior buyer runs the certificate-expiry report (MAN-PUR-72 §22.6) on the first working day of each month with 90 days as the window, and writes to every supplier whose UN 38.3 certificate expires inside it.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "All provisions of POL-SUP-003 §4 other than §4.4 remain in full effect.",
          "quote": "Every other part of POL-SUP-003 §4 stands.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "pol-sup-003",
      "type": "policy",
      "title": "POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact": "Effective 1 September 2026 via AMD-SUP-2026-02, clause 4.4 is amended to mandate that UN 38.3 certificates must be issued within the last 12 months and maintain a valid-to date at least 60 days beyond the purchase order placement date.",
          "quote": "With effect from 1 September 2026, Supplier Policy POL-SUP-003 §4.4 is replaced by the following: \"A UN 38.3 certificate is accepted only if it was issued within the last 12 months, and its valid-to date is at least 60 days after the date the order is placed.\"",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "Battery certificates issued under the older 24-month validity rule are treated as having no certificate for any orders placed on or after 1 September 2026.",
          "quote": "A certificate that meets the old rule (issued within 24 months and not expired) but not the new one counts as no certificate for new orders from 1 September 2026.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "topic-un-38-3-certificates",
      "type": "topic",
      "title": "UN 38.3 Certificates",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact": "Since 1 September 2026 under AMD-SUP-2026-02, UN 38.3 certificates for lithium-cell parts are only accepted if issued within the preceding 12 months with a validity extending at least 60 days past order date.",
          "quote": "A UN 38.3 certificate is accepted only if it was issued within the last 12 months, and its valid-to date is at least 60 days after the date the order is placed.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "1. What changes",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        },
        {
          "fact": "The senior buyer executes the certificate-expiry report (MAN-PUR-72 §22.6) on the first working day of each month using a 90-day threshold to notify suppliers of impending UN 38.3 expirations.",
          "quote": "The senior buyer runs the certificate-expiry report (MAN-PUR-72 §22.6) on the first working day of each month with 90 days as the window, and writes to every supplier whose UN 38.3 certificate expires inside it.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "role-pur-sr",
      "type": "role",
      "title": "Role PUR-SR",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact": "The senior buyer is required to run the certificate-expiry report per MAN-PUR-72 §22.6 on the first working day of every month with a 90-day window and notify suppliers with expiring UN 38.3 certificates.",
          "quote": "The senior buyer runs the certificate-expiry report (MAN-PUR-72 §22.6) on the first working day of each month with 90 days as the window, and writes to every supplier whose UN 38.3 certificate expires inside it.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "items-bat",
      "type": "item-family",
      "title": "BAT Item Family",
      "facts": [
        {
          "fact": "Raising purchase orders for lithium battery components requires verifying that the UN 38.3 certificate was issued within 12 months and remains valid for at least 60 days post-order placement.",
          "quote": "Before raising an order for a lithium-cell part, check the certificate's issue date and its valid-to date against the new rule.",
          "page": 1,
          "section": "3. What purchase staff must do",
          "sheet": null,
          "row": null
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    {
      "kind": "superseded",
      "other": "POL-SUP-003",
      "detail": "AMD-SUP-2026-02 §1.1 explicitly replaces clause §4.4 of POL-SUP-003, reducing UN 38.3 certificate validity from 24 months to 12 months and requiring at least 60 days of validity remaining after PO placement."
    }
  ]
}
